  "scope": "# Review \u2014 424c822d69f3\n\nAssignment `review-ec54eded9d66352d`; production generator `2.2.0`, SHA-256 `6f2a8be446d2bb9e96302063bcb891fbe1459f128607995ffbdef49487e3825a`, unchanged.\nChange: added a task-local **proposed/unapproved** `selection_mode` prototype with `nearest` (canonical default) and `farthest`; production and canonical authority are untouched.\nCanonical Racket SHA-256 remains `1379212df45efd44f4bb6d4cafca92b9588442bfc83807ed5d926d3048ccade5`; farthest SHA-256 is `01f1655af7c3e059e944456de586dee78c76a464f99595fb68a6af9e748fae55`.\nPaired seeds share inputs, one setting is fixed per episode, defaults are 3 demonstrations + 4 distinct queries, and both counts support 1\u20138 independently.\nThe sampler rejects nearest or farthest distance ties; every retained demonstration and query refutes the alternate setting through actual Racket execution.\nPublic files contain only visible demonstrations and query inputs; opaque IDs hash the exact bytes written. Settings, seeds, programs, provenance, rivals, and query labels stay private.\nA reusable source-bound verifier checks retained/current prototype, verifier, and generator identities; validates report/source bindings; rejects undeclared files and semantic tampering; reconstructs public projections; and replays 14 episode labels plus 4 canonical pairs through Racket.\nFocused verification: 118/118 tests pass (`37` prototype/verifier + `81` existing task tests). Evidence: `checks/final-focused-tests.log`.\nRuntime evidence: `checks/parametric/nearest-farthest-v1/`; bounded adversarial result: `checks/parametric/adversarial.json`.\nA latent test-helper typo (`center2`) was repaired to `center` with a hand-checked tie regression; no production behavior changed.",
